      ":question/worked-solution": "To transform $A$ into $B,$ we need to make the entries below $a_{13}=-2$ equal to $0.$\n\nTo do this, we can apply the following elementary row operations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}-9 & -2 & -2 \\\\ 4 & -5 & -8 \\\\ -8 & -1 & -12\\end{bmatrix}\n\\xrightarrow{R_{2}:=R_{2}-4R_{1}}\\begin{bmatrix}-9 & -2 & -2 \\\\ 40 & 3 & 0 \\\\ -8 & -1 & -12\\end{bmatrix}\n\\xrightarrow{R_{3}:=R_{3}-6R_{1}}\\begin{bmatrix}-9 & -2 & -2 \\\\ 40 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 46 & 11 & 0\\end{bmatrix}=B\n$$\n\nTherefore, the elementary row operations are\n\n$R_{2}:=R_{2}-4R_{1}$ and $R_{3}:=R_{3}-6R_{1}$.",
